      "player": "DSV3 Valley",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Great! Now I'm in my first turn's postcombat main phase (though we haven't had combat yet - this might be a naming quirk). I have 3 lands in hand that I can play, but I can only play one land per turn. Looking at my options:\n\
\n\
1. Mountain (id=p5)\n\
2. Mountain (id=p6) \n\
3. Thriving Bluff (id=p9)\n\
\n\
Since Thriving Bluff enters tapped, if I play it now, it won't produce mana this turn. However, I don't have any 1-mana plays anyway. My first playable spell is Heartfire Immolator or Thermo-Alchemist for 2 mana on turn 2.\n\
\n\
Strategy: I should play a Mountain now so I can have both Mountains and Thriving Bluff available next turn. That gives me RR available on turn 2 to cast either Heartfire Immolator or Thermo-Alchemist, and Thriving Bluff can come in tapped on turn 2 to give me a third mana source for turn 3.\n\
\n\
Actually, wait - if I play Thriving Bluff now (enters tapped), I won't be able to use it until turn 2 anyway. But if I play Mountain now, I'll have 1 untapped Mountain on turn 2, and could play Thriving Bluff tapped on turn 2, giving me RR total on turn 2 (Mountain + Thriving Bluff producing R), which is enough for my 2-mana spells.\n\
\n\
But if I play Mountain now, then on turn 2 I could play the other Mountain (untapped) AND Thriving Bluff (tapped), giving me RR from the Mountains plus another R from Thriving Bluff next turn. That's better mana development.\n\
\n\
So I'll play a Mountain now.\n\
\n\
